Z||000004||Fiero-lite||05-24-2000||06:01 PM||||Interesting topic.  I am having the same problem!  I have a 1988 GT that never got the recall mods.  I've been back and forth so many times with two local dealers, the NHTSA  amd PM  CARES (PM WHO CARES!) that I could do the mods myself if I had the parts and a shop.  I'm restoring  my car and would like to reduce the chance of an engine fire (who wouldn't).  BTW- the SAFETY recalls DO NOT expire.  I'm trying to go higher with this issue, so please e-mail me if you are experiencing this problem also.  Anyone can reach me directly at    bob@solustech.com<BR>I received my info on the recall at the site below. <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/v6recall.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/v6recall.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||11
